Fuel Economy Predictor
========================================================
author: Your Name
date: October 2026
autosize: true
transition: rotate
font-family: 'Helvetica'

A Shiny app that predicts a car's MPG from weight, horsepower and transmission

**App:** https://YOUR-ACCOUNT.shinyapps.io/mpg-predictor/

The Problem
========================================================

- Fuel cost is one of the biggest running costs of owning a car
- Buyers often know a car's **weight**, **horsepower** and **transmission**, but not its real-world MPG
- We want a quick, simple estimate that needs **no statistics knowledge**

The **Fuel Economy Predictor** turns three easy inputs into an MPG estimate with an uncertainty range.

The Model (evaluated live)
========================================================

Linear regression on R's built-in `mtcars` data:

```{r}
fit <- lm(mpg ~ wt + hp + am, data = mtcars)
round(coef(fit), 3)
round(summary(fit)$r.squared, 3)
```

The three inputs explain about `r round(100 * summary(fit)$r.squared)`% of the variation in MPG.

Example Prediction
========================================================
left: 55%

```{r, echo=FALSE, fig.width=6, fig.height=4.5}
fit <- lm(mpg ~ wt + hp + am, data = mtcars)
plot(mtcars$wt, mtcars$mpg, pch = 19, col = "grey40",
     xlab = "Weight (1000 lbs)", ylab = "MPG")
g <- seq(1.5, 5.5, 0.05)
lines(g, predict(fit, data.frame(wt = g, hp = 140, am = 0)), col = "steelblue", lwd = 2)
lines(g, predict(fit, data.frame(wt = g, hp = 140, am = 1)), col = "darkorange", lwd = 2, lty = 2)
p <- predict(fit, data.frame(wt = 3.2, hp = 140, am = 0))
points(3.2, p, pch = 19, col = "red", cex = 2)
```

***

A 3,200 lb automatic car with 140 hp:

```{r, echo=FALSE}
car <- data.frame(wt = 3.2, hp = 140, am = 0)
round(predict(fit, car, interval = "prediction"), 1)
```

The app shows this instantly and redraws as you move the sliders.

Why Use It?
========================================================

- **Simple:** two sliders, one radio button, one checkbox
- **Instant:** predictions update reactively on every change
- **Honest:** shows a 95% prediction interval, not just a single number
- **Documented:** a built-in *How to use* tab explains every control

Try it: **https://YOUR-ACCOUNT.shinyapps.io/mpg-predictor/**

Code: **https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/mpg-predictor**
